      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4xOA5mfGY44X"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Task B1: Convert Numbers to Padded Strings\n",
        "\n",
        "**Direction:** Implement `to_string(X, y, n_numbers, largest)` that:\n",
        "- Joins each input list like `[3, 10]` into the string `\"3+10\"`, padded on the left with spaces to fixed length\n",
        "- Converts each sum integer to a right-padded string of fixed length\n",
        "- Input max length formula: `n_numbers * ceil(log10(largest+1)) + n_numbers - 1`\n",
        "- Output max length formula: `ceil(log10(n_numbers * (largest+1)))`\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Why padding?** LSTMs require fixed-length input sequences. Padding with spaces allows variable-length numbers to be handled uniformly. The model learns to ignore the padding character."
      ],
      "id": "4xOA5mfGY44X"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 20,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
